<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gnaeus Julius Agricola</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">40–93</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Agricola</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gnaeus Julius Agricola was a Roman general and governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> from about 77 to 84 CE. He completed the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> by crushing the Ordovices and taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglesey">Anglesey</a>, then campaigned in northern Britain and defeated the Caledonians at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mons">Mons</a> Graupius. His son-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a> wrote his biography, the Agricola, the main source for his career.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gnaeus-julius-agricola.jpg" alt="Gnaeus Julius Agricola" width="320" height="779" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ad Meskens · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_baths_julius_agricola_01.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
